# UI Approach: Hand-Rolled Tailwind, Not shadcn Components

**This rule previously described a shadcn/ui-heavy component system (Table, Tabs,
Alert, Dialog, Command, Progress, Skeleton, Tooltip, `components/dashboard/metric-card.tsx`).
None of that exists in this repo.** It was copied from the Casimir Intelligence
product app and never matched this marketing site. Fixed July 2026; if you're
reading an older version of this file elsewhere, disregard it for this repo.

## What's actually true here

- Every page (`app/**/page.tsx`) is built with **inline `style={{}}` objects
  plus Tailwind utility classes**, not shadcn primitives. Zero pages import
  from `@/components/ui`.
- `components/ui/` does have a partial shadcn install: `badge`, `button`,
  `card`, `input`, `label`, `navigation-menu`, `select`, `separator`, `sheet`,
  `textarea`. These exist but are **not the house convention**; don't assume
  more shadcn components are available just because `components.json` exists.
- The real, established convention for anything visual (badges, cards,
  section chrome) is a **small set of hand-built domain components** in
  `components/`, not a generic component library:
  - `components/risk-badge.tsx`: `RiskBadge`, `TrlBadge`, `StatusBadge`,
    `ComplianceBadge`. Reach for these before inventing a new inline colored
    `<span>` badge; see `.cursor/rules/design-tokens.mdc` for when to use
    which.
  - `components/scroll-reveal.tsx`: `ScrollReveal`, `StaggerReveal` for
    entrance animation on scroll. Every content section on every page wraps
    its content in one of these.
  - `components/nav.tsx` and `components/footer.tsx`: shared page chrome.

## When to build a new component vs. inline

- If a pattern repeats 3+ times across pages (a badge variant, a card shape),
  extract it into `components/<name>.tsx` following the existing style
  (inline `style` objects, not a new CSS-in-JS or styled-components
  approach).
- If it's page-specific and used once, inline styling directly in the page
  file is the house convention, not an anti-pattern to avoid.
- Don't introduce shadcn `Table`, `Tabs`, `Alert`, `Dialog`, etc. into this
  repo without discussing it first; the whole site is deliberately
  hand-styled to match the "Illuminated Intelligence" design system (see
  `.cursor/rules/design-tokens.mdc`), and shadcn's default styling doesn't
  match it out of the box.
